From b6d7542a1cf6fbbafea595a07e59bdfcc7bf7598 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:52:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(view): defer the release re-home until the deform
 settles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A drag reparents the view under the unclipped drag tree so the sheet spans
outputs; the release re-homed it under the home output's clipped root
immediately, while the physics spring still displaced the sheet past that
clip — the window's own border ring was cut off at the edge the moment the
move ended, and only fitted the edge again once the deform settled.

The resting re-home now waits in View::setSceneParent while the sheet is
displaced. The deferral window spans the whole release flow — endDragPhysics
arms it, the first animation tick closes it — so a drop that chains reparents
(a cross-workspace transfer parks under the server tree, then re-homes onto
the destination layer) still lands in the wait, while a later state change
(fullscreen, pin, scratchpad) applies immediately and drops it. The wait is
applied in the same tick the spring settles, or earlier while an overview is
open and its cards need the home tree; the unmap path lands it too so a
remap cannot reappear unclipped under the drag tree.

Pinned by drag/physics_release_settle (outputs=2): a same-workspace drop and
a cross-workspace transfer drop — the sheet's far half keeps drawing on the
neighbour output through the displaced samples (16/64 ms), then the home clip
applies again after the settle. Both failure branches are falsified: red on
this base before the fix, red on a consume-once-arm mutation (the transfer
cut), red on an apply-neutered mutation (the clip never applied).

Validated: meson units 142/142; harness drag/ 29/30 — the one failure,
drag/floating_release_settle ('did not animate through the margin'),
reproduces identically on a pristine base build and predates this change;
clang-format --dry-run -Werror clean.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
