From 8a3c231da30bfd6a7aa24b3fe7aaae3acf7e8317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:16:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(view): demote the drag tree only when its last
 drag-presented view leaves

The F1-F8 round moved the drag-tree demotion into setSceneParent's
leaving hook, where it fired whenever ANY view left the drag tree. A
settling release or an elevated transient child unmapping then demoted
the shared drag tree mid-drag of another window, dropping the held
window behind fullscreen/pinned until its own release (Talia P2).

The elevation now serves the whole drag presentation: transient
children follow the departing view home first, and the demotion waits
until no view remains under the drag tree. Pinned by the new
drag/settle_overlap_drag check, which freezes the animation clock
between the two grabs so the overlap cannot race away; red-first
verified (held green 6400 -> overlap 0 without the gate).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/view/view.cpp                             |  23 +++-
 src/view/view.h                               |   2 +
 .../checks/drag/settle_overlap_drag.sh        | 128 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/harness/checks/drag/settle_overlap_drag.sh

